</translation_old>
<translation_old translation_old="And he got up immediately without telling any of his disciples, and came upon the harbor of the sea which he'd been told about in the revelation. Right away, he'd found that the holy Apa Lucius had come down from the ship. When they embraced each other, the old man said to him, “Did I not tell you, my son, that I hoped in Christ that wherever you go I would come to you?” Then they glorified God for making them worthy to see each other and fulfilling what is written: “There the deer met. They saw the faces of one another, and came out in number, and not one of them fell, for the Lord commanded them, and his Spirit gathered them together.”">
<verse_n_old verse_n_old="4">
